@relkit/docs:test: Received: "---\ntitle: Local Docker services\ndescription: Run graph-required Redis and MinIO recipes with immutable image versions and project-scoped lifecycle commands.\n---\n\n`@relkit/docker` is a local-service materializer, not a deployment target. `check` writes a deterministic plan\nwithout contacting Docker. `dev` then starts only the recipes required by the checked graph, waits for their\nhealth checks, and supplies their outputs to the matching binding.\n\n## Current bundled images\n\nThe integration packages pin both a readable tag and an immutable digest. A RELKIT package release therefore\nselects an exact local-service image rather than whatever a mutable tag points to later.\n\n| Adapter    | Image tag                                          | Immutable digest                                                          |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Redis      | `redis:7.4.2-alpine`                               | `sha256:02419de7eddf55aa5bcf49efb74e88fa8d931b4d77c07eff8a6b2144472b6952` |\n| S3 / MinIO | `quay.io/minio/minio:RELEASE.2025-04-22T22-12-26Z` | `sha256:a1ea29fa28355559ef137d71fc570e508a214ec84ff8083e39bc5428980b015e` |\n\nRELKIT discovers the Docker server version at startup but does not currently enforce a minimum engine\nversion. Use a maintained Docker Engine or Docker Desktop release with the `docker` CLI available on `PATH`:\n\n```sh\ndocker version\nbun run relkit local status\n```\n\n## Select local recipes\n\nUse `docker(redis())` or `docker(s3())` for a local-only binding. Wrap a configured connected adapter when\ndevelopment should use Docker while release builds resolve named binding values. The Redis and storage guides\nshow both forms in the commerce application.\n\nDocker starts Redis with a persistent `/data` volume and waits for `redis-cli PING`. MinIO receives generated\nproject-local credentials, persists `/data`, waits for its readiness endpoint, and initializes the `relkit`\nbucket. Both publish random loopback ports instead of claiming fixed host ports.\n\n## File-backed events and jobs\n\nLocal event and job profiles do not use Docker. `localEvent()` and `localJob()` from `@relkit/local` register\nthe existing durable filesystem runtimes and store their state under `.relkit/state` by default. The `event`,\n`event-function`, and `job` add commands reuse compatible profiles; a full service bundle creates these local\nprofiles when no configured defaults exist. See the [Local API](/docs/api/integrations/local) for direct\nauthoring. Use a different `root` only when the application needs an isolated local state directory.\n\n## Control the project lifecycle\n\n```sh\nbun run relkit local up --detach\nbun run relkit local status\nbun run dev --local=off\nbun run relkit local stop\nbun run relkit local reset --yes\n```\n\nHealthy services and volumes survive source reloads. `stop` stops this project's labelled services; `reset`\nalso removes its validated volumes and override state. It refuses a live attached lease and never targets\nanother checkout. Docker is not contacted by `build`, deployment preview, or deployment apply.\n\n<include cwd>content/generated/related/integrations-local-docker.mdx</include>\n"
